 ## Install
 
+Tier-1 platforms: macOS (arm64), Ubuntu 22.04+, and Arch Linux. Every release ships self-contained, vendored-Ruby binaries — no system Ruby required — as checksummed GitHub Releases assets.
+
+Pick one channel:
+
+```bash
+# Homebrew (macOS)
+brew install ivankuznetsov/hive/hive
+
+# Arch Linux
+yay -S hive-bin          # or: paru -S hive-bin / makepkg from the AUR PKGBUILD
+
+# One-liner (any tier-1 platform)
+curl -fsSL https://github.com/ivankuznetsov/hive/releases/latest/download/install.sh | bash
+```
+
+**Command name:** if Apache Hive already owns `hive` on your PATH, installers fall back to the name `hv` automatically (`HIVE_BIN_NAME=hv` pre-seeds this for the one-liner).
+
+**Via your coding agent:** paste [install.md](install.md) into Claude Code, Codex, or Pi — it detects your OS, picks the best channel, verifies `hive --version`, offers `hive init`, and installs skills through your agent's marketplace.
+
+**Updating / removing:** `hive update` shells out to your install channel's native updater (brew upgrade / yay -Syu hive-bin / re-run of the one-liner); it never swaps the binary in place. `hive uninstall` removes the daemon registration plus project scaffolds you confirm — accumulated state under `~/.local/state/hive/` and project work are always preserved. Agent skills live in a separate marketplace package ([packaging/skills/README.md](packaging/skills/README.md)) and are managed through each agent's own plugin flow.
