+      (the cwd's own plus registered projects under the cwd), prompting
+      before removing each one. Non-interactive runs keep everything.
+
+      NEVER deleted: ~/.local/state/hive/, ~/.local/share/hive/, and any
+      project work outside the scaffolds you confirm. --purge additionally
+      removes ~/.config/hive/ and ~/.cache/hive/ but still preserves state.
+
+      The binary itself is owned by your install channel:
+        brew    → run `brew uninstall ivankuznetsov/hive/hive` afterwards
+        aur     → run `sudo pacman -Rns hive-bin` afterwards
+        script  → removed for you (~/.local/bin/hive and the hv fallback)
+
+      Agent skills/plugins are distributed through each coding agent's own
+      marketplace and are left untouched — remove them from each agent's
+      plugin management separately.
+    DESC
+    option :purge, type: :boolean, default: false,
+                   desc: "also remove ~/.config/hive and ~/.cache/hive (state is still preserved)"
+    option :yes, type: :boolean, default: false, aliases: [:y],
+                 desc: "assume yes for project-scaffold removal prompts"
+    def uninstall
+      require "hive/commands/uninstall"
+      Hive::Commands::Uninstall.new(purge: options[:purge], yes: options[:yes]).call
+      $stdout.puts "hive uninstall: done."
     end
 
     desc "forget NAME", "Remove a project from the global registry (inverse of `hive init`)"
