diff --git a/wiki/modules/packaging.md b/wiki/modules/packaging.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e2b4d4c14
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wiki/modules/packaging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+---
+title: Packaging & Installation
+type: module
+created: 2026-08-25
+tags: [packaging, install, release, xdg]
+---
+
+**TLDR**: How hive is packaged, released, installed, updated, and uninstalled. Implements plan "Hive Packaging & Installation v1" (U1–U8).
+
+## Release pipeline (U1)
+
+- `.github/workflows/release.yml` — tag-push (`v*`) build matrix: macos-14 (arm64) + ubuntu-22.04. Verifies the tag equals `Hive::VERSION`, builds via `packaging/build.sh` (Tebako → vendored-Ruby single-file binary), smoke-tests `--version`, generates `SHA256SUMS` (`packaging/checksums.sh`), publishes a GitHub Release. Releases are the canonical artifact source for every channel.
+- `packaging/tebako.yml` — Tebako packaging config; entrypoint stays `bin/hive`.
+- Fallback ladder: tebako → portable-Ruby tarball (`BUILD_TARBALL_FALLBACK=1` + `PORTABLE_RUBY_URL`).
+
+## Install channels
+
+| Channel | Files | Update path | Marker |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| brew tap | `packaging/homebrew/Formula/hive.rb` (+ `.github/workflows/tap-bump.yml`, `packaging/tap-bump.sh`) | `brew upgrade ivankuznetsov/hive/hive` | `brew` |
+| AUR | `packaging/aur/PKGBUILD`, `.SRCINFO`, `bump.sh` | `yay -Syu hive-bin` | `aur` |
+| one-liner | `packaging/install.sh` | re-run of install.sh | `script` |
+
+Each installer writes the channel into `~/.config/hive/install-channel`; `hive update` ([[commands/update]]) refuses to act when the marker is missing/unknown instead of guessing (never swaps the binary in place).
+
+## CLI surface (U5)
+
+- [[commands/update]] — channel-native upgrade.
+- [[commands/uninstall]] — prompted, project-scoped removal; never deletes `~/.local/state/hive/` or work artifacts, even with `--purge`.
+- `lib/hive/install_layout.rb` — XDG resolution: bin `~/.local/bin`, config `~/.config/hive/`, data `~/.local/share/hive/`, state `~/.local/state/hive/`, cache `~/.cache/hive/`. Honors XDG_* env vars. Includes copy-then-rename migration of legacy `~/.hive-state/` (backup at `<dir>.migrated-backup`; never deletes on failure).
+- `lib/hive/name_conflict.rb` — Apache Hive on PATH ⇒ installs use the fallback name `hv`.
+
+## Service registration (U6)
+
+`lib/hive/service.rb` factory → `Launchd` (plist at `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.hive.daemon.plist`, `launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID`) or `SystemdUser` (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/systemd/user/hive.service`). Templates live in `packaging/service/*.erb`. Registration is opt-in: `hive init --start-daemon[=bool]` / `HIVE_INIT_DAEMON=yes|no`, TTY prompt otherwise, non-TTY defaults to skip. WSL2 without systemd degrades to an actionable manual-start hint.
+
+## Prompt installer + skills (U7/U8)
+
+- Root `install.md` — defensive agent-pasted prompt (detect OS → pick channel → verify → offer init → marketplace-only skills).
+- `packaging/skills/` — extraction source for the separate `<org>/hive-skills` repo (`.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` day-one for Claude Code). Core binary and init contain zero skill-writing logic.
